# The local override every env template points a credential at. It needs its
# own rule: `*.env` above matches a name ending in `.env`, and these end in
# `.local`, so nothing here reached them and `git add -A` would have staged a
# real key. Whole family, not just docker's -- the agents ship `.env.example`
# files that ask for the same neighbour, and the wheel publisher already treats
# a packaged `.env.local` as a leaked secret.
*.env.local
key.env
# The Compose template, and the only env file in the repo. It carries settings
# and empty placeholders, never a credential -- a real key belongs in
# docker/.env.local, which the `*.env.local` rule above ignores.
!docker/.env
sty_readme.md
CLAUDE.local.md
